<div class="manifest-panel">
  <article class="route-file" aria-labelledby="route-file-title">
    <header>
      <div>
        <span>.wt / 01</span>
        <h3 id="route-file-title">database-primary.wt</h3>
      </div>
      <strong>WarpTweet route</strong>
    </header>
    <dl>
      <div>
        <dt>From</dt>
        <dd>
          <code>127.0.0.1:15432</code>
          <small>Local listener on Machine A</small>
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Via</dt>
        <dd>
          <code>server.example:2222</code>
          <small>WarpTweet server endpoint</small>
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>To</dt>
        <dd>
          <code>127.0.0.1:5432</code>
          <small>Declared service on Machine B</small>
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Profile</dt>
        <dd>
          Hybrid / 01
          <small>ML-KEM-768 + X25519 · ML-DSA-44 + Ed25519</small>
        </dd>
      </div>
    </dl>
  </article>

  <div class="manifest-anatomy">
    <p>
      The CLI generates and validates the route manifest. Hybrid identities remain protected on
      their machines.
    </p>
    <dl>
      <div><dt>Profile</dt><dd>The exact hybrid suite both ends must share</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Server</dt><dd>The remote WarpTweet endpoint</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Tunnel ID</dt><dd>The name used by the CLI</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Listen</dt><dd>The local application address</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Target</dt><dd>The remote service address</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Supervision</dt><dd>The connection recovery policy</dd></div>
    </dl>
    <a href="/schemas/client-tunnels-v1.schema.json">Read the client schema</a>
  </div>
</div>
